== Their relationship ==

The Four Foundations investigate the philosophical questions beneath the undertaking. The Manifesto articulates the direction and necessity of the undertaking. The Charter expresses the commitments by which it is pursued. The Constitution identifies what must not be sacrificed in its pursuit.

'''The four philosophical foundations are not the four conditions examined in the Manifesto.''' They address different questions and should remain conceptually distinct.

These writings are meant to be read together. Their roles differ, but their purpose is shared: to make BITwiki's direction, reasoning, responsibilities, and enduring commitments intelligible to the people who encounter, study, and develop it.

